{"SurveyEntry":{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","SurveyName":"AI Attestation Trust Study","SurveyDescription":null,"SurveyOwnerID":"UR_5jZ326t4zwQh5S6","SurveyBrandID":"gatech","DivisionID":null,"SurveyLanguage":"EN","SurveyActiveResponseSet":"RS_1Hcv7gup4F7ws9U","SurveyStatus":"Active","SurveyStartDate":"0000-00-00 00:00:00","SurveyExpirationDate":"0000-00-00 00:00:00","SurveyCreationDate":"2026-06-19 22:30:03","CreatorID":"UR_5jZ326t4zwQh5S6","LastModified":"2026-06-22 14:41:57","LastAccessed":"0000-00-00 00:00:00","LastActivated":"2026-06-22 12:45:35","Deleted":null},"SurveyElements":[{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"BL","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Blocks","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"0":{"Type":"Default","Description":"Consent","ID":"BL_881io0YoXtLYmSa","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}},"1":{"Type":"Trash","Description":"Trash \/ Unused Questions","ID":"BL_3BZVrqy1BSFNT7g","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID12"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID13"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID14"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID15"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID7"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID8"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID10"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID16"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID41"}]},"2":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Instructions","ID":"BL_3UW8olS4EWG8PrM","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID2"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}},"3":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Demographics","ID":"BL_3TWOL5FptLlSgVo","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID5"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID4"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID3"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID6"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}},"4":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Trial 1","ID":"BL_8o8SFUxZ5gNrSwm","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID17"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID18"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID19"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID20"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","Looping":"Static","LoopingOptions":{"Static":{"1":{"1":"1","2":"7","3":"low","4":"If an online store can\u2019t ship my order by the promised date, can it just delay the order without asking me?","5":"No. If it cannot ship on time, it generally must get your consent to the delay or promptly refund your money.","6":"none","7":"correct","8":""},"2":{"1":"1","2":"8","3":"low","4":"For a credit card, how long before the due date must the bill generally be sent or delivered?","5":"The bill generally must be mailed or delivered at least 14 days before the payment due date.","6":"none","7":"incorrect","8":""},"3":{"1":"1","2":"9","3":"low","4":"How long does First-Class Mail usually take for letters and postcards in the U.S.?","5":"First-Class Mail for letters and postcards is generally delivered in 1 to 5 business days.","6":"weak","7":"correct","8":"Source: United States Postal Service \u2014 USPS, First-Class Mail, delivery standard for letters and postcards"},"4":{"1":"1","2":"10","3":"low","4":"If I book a U.S. flight directly with an airline at least a week before departure, can I cancel within 24 hours for a full refund?","5":"No. For a full refund, you generally must have bought it at least fourteen days before departure and cancel within 12 hours.","6":"weak","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: U.S. Department of Transportation \u2014 DOT Aviation Consumer Protection, Refunds and 24-hour reservation requirement"},"5":{"1":"1","2":"11","3":"low","4":"When substituting dried herbs for fresh herbs in a recipe, what ratio should I use?","5":"Use about 1 teaspoon of dried herbs for each 1 tablespoon of fresh herbs.","6":"strong","7":"correct","8":"Source: University of Nebraska-Lincoln Extension \u2014 Nebraska Extension, using herbs and spices in cooking, fresh-to-dried herb substitution guidance<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (University of Nebraska-Lincoln Extension) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"6":{"1":"1","2":"12","3":"low","4":"Which Great Lake has the greatest maximum depth?","5":"Lake Michigan has the greatest maximum depth, at about 1,332 feet.","6":"strong","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: U.S. Environmental Protection Agency \u2014 EPA, Great Lakes Facts and Figures, maximum depth table<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (U.S. Environmental Protection Agency) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"7":{"1":"1","2":"1","3":"high","4":"If I take money out of a traditional IRA before age 59\u00bd and no exception applies, what extra federal tax usually applies?","5":"The extra federal tax is generally 10% of the taxable part of the early distribution.","6":"none","7":"correct","8":""},"8":{"1":"1","2":"2","3":"high","4":"What is the maximum total acetaminophen an adult should take in one day from all medicines combined?","5":"The adult maximum is 5,000 mg in 24 hours from all acetaminophen-containing medicines.","6":"none","7":"incorrect","8":""},"9":{"1":"1","2":"3","3":"high","4":"How long can cooked leftovers stay safely in the refrigerator before I should throw them out?","5":"Cooked leftovers are generally safe in the refrigerator for 3 to 4 days.","6":"weak","7":"correct","8":"Source: U.S. Department of Agriculture Food Safety and Inspection Service \u2014 USDA FSIS, Leftovers and Food Safety, guidance on refrigerated leftovers"},"10":{"1":"1","2":"4","3":"high","4":"For important online accounts, which is generally stronger against phishing: a FIDO security key or a text-message code?","5":"A text-message code is generally stronger against phishing than a FIDO security key.","6":"weak","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency \u2014 CISA, Implementing Phishing-Resistant MFA, discussion of FIDO\/WebAuthn authentication"},"11":{"1":"1","2":"5","3":"high","4":"If I enroll late in Medicare Part B and don\u2019t qualify for a Special Enrollment Period, how is the late enrollment penalty usually figured?","5":"It is usually 10% for each full 12-month period you could have had Part B but did not, and it usually lasts as long as you have Part B.","6":"strong","7":"correct","8":"Source: Medicare.gov \u2014 Medicare.gov, Avoid late enrollment penalties, Part B late enrollment penalty<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (Medicare.gov) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"12":{"1":"1","2":"6","3":"high","4":"If the IRS mails me a notice of deficiency, how long do I generally have to file a petition with the U.S. Tax Court?","5":"You generally have 120 days from the notice date to file a Tax Court petition, or 180 days if the notice is addressed outside the United States.","6":"strong","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: United States Tax Court \u2014 U.S. Tax Court, Starting a Case, deadline for filing a petition after a notice of deficiency<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (United States Tax Court) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"}},"Randomization":"All"},"BlockVisibility":"Collapsed"}},"5":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Baseline Trust","ID":"BL_2b2CxWbu39U4c1U","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID9"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}},"6":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Debrief","ID":"BL_aXnT6T9tRTehsRE","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID11"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID42"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID43"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}},"8":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Trial 2","ID":"BL_50vtbL8ZxZ3bjCK","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID21"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID22"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID23"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID24"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":false,"RandomizeQuestions":"false","Looping":"Static","LoopingOptions":{"Static":{"2":{"1":"2","2":"7","3":"low","4":"If an online store can\u2019t ship my order by the promised date, can it just delay the order without asking me?","5":"Yes. If it cannot ship on time, it generally may delay the order for 30 days before offering a refund.","6":"none","7":"incorrect","8":""},"3":{"1":"2","2":"8","3":"low","4":"For a credit card, how long before the due date must the bill generally be sent or delivered?","5":"The bill generally must be mailed or delivered at least 21 days before the payment due date.","6":"weak","7":"correct","8":"Source: Consumer Financial Protection Bureau \u2014 CFPB Ask CFPB, How long before my credit card payment due date does the card issuer have to mail or deliver my bill?"},"4":{"1":"2","2":"9","3":"low","4":"How long does First-Class Mail usually take for letters and postcards in the U.S.?","5":"First-Class Mail for letters and postcards is generally delivered in 2 to 7 business days.","6":"weak","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: United States Postal Service \u2014 USPS, First-Class Mail, delivery standard for letters and postcards"},"5":{"1":"2","2":"10","3":"low","4":"If I book a U.S. flight directly with an airline at least a week before departure, can I cancel within 24 hours for a full refund?","5":"Yes. If you bought it at least seven days before departure, the airline generally must let you cancel within 24 hours for a full refund.","6":"strong","7":"correct","8":"Source: U.S. Department of Transportation \u2014 DOT Aviation Consumer Protection, Refunds and 24-hour reservation requirement<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (U.S. Department of Transportation) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"6":{"1":"2","2":"11","3":"low","4":"When substituting dried herbs for fresh herbs in a recipe, what ratio should I use?","5":"Use about 2 teaspoons of dried herbs for each 1 tablespoon of fresh herbs.","6":"strong","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: University of Nebraska-Lincoln Extension \u2014 Nebraska Extension, using herbs and spices in cooking, fresh-to-dried herb substitution guidance<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (University of Nebraska-Lincoln Extension) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"7":{"1":"2","2":"12","3":"low","4":"Which Great Lake has the greatest maximum depth?","5":"Lake Superior has the greatest maximum depth, at about 1,332 feet.","6":"none","7":"correct","8":""},"8":{"1":"2","2":"1","3":"high","4":"If I take money out of a traditional IRA before age 59\u00bd and no exception applies, what extra federal tax usually applies?","5":"The extra federal tax is generally 15% of the taxable part of the early distribution.","6":"none","7":"incorrect","8":""},"9":{"1":"2","2":"2","3":"high","4":"What is the maximum total acetaminophen an adult should take in one day from all medicines combined?","5":"The adult maximum is 4,000 mg in 24 hours from all acetaminophen-containing medicines.","6":"weak","7":"correct","8":"Source: U.S. Food and Drug Administration \u2014 FDA, Acetaminophen Information, consumer safety information on maximum daily dose"},"10":{"1":"2","2":"3","3":"high","4":"How long can cooked leftovers stay safely in the refrigerator before I should throw them out?","5":"Cooked leftovers are generally safe in the refrigerator for 5 to 6 days.","6":"weak","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: U.S. Department of Agriculture Food Safety and Inspection Service \u2014 USDA FSIS, Leftovers and Food Safety, guidance on refrigerated leftovers"},"11":{"1":"2","2":"4","3":"high","4":"For important online accounts, which is generally stronger against phishing: a FIDO security key or a text-message code?","5":"A FIDO security key is generally stronger against phishing than a text-message code.","6":"strong","7":"correct","8":"Source: Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency \u2014 CISA, Implementing Phishing-Resistant MFA, discussion of FIDO\/WebAuthn authentication<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"12":{"1":"2","2":"5","3":"high","4":"If I enroll late in Medicare Part B and don\u2019t qualify for a Special Enrollment Period, how is the late enrollment penalty usually figured?","5":"It is usually 5% for each full 12-month period you could have had Part B but did not, and it usually lasts for the first three years of Part B.","6":"strong","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: Medicare.gov \u2014 Medicare.gov, Avoid late enrollment penalties, Part B late enrollment penalty<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (Medicare.gov) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"13":{"1":"2","2":"6","3":"high","4":"If the IRS mails me a notice of deficiency, how long do I generally have to file a petition with the U.S. Tax Court?","5":"You generally have 90 days from the notice date to file a Tax Court petition, or 150 days if the notice is addressed outside the United States.","6":"none","7":"correct","8":""}},"Randomization":"All"},"Blo