alse,"RandomizeQuestions":"false","Looping":"Static","LoopingOptions":{"Static":{"38":{"1":"5","2":"7","3":"low","4":"If an online store can\u2019t ship my order by the promised date, can it just delay the order without asking me?","5":"No. If it cannot ship on time, it generally must get your consent to the delay or promptly refund your money.","6":"strong","7":"correct","8":"Source: Federal Trade Commission \u2014 FTC, Business Guide to the Mail, Internet, or Telephone Order Merchandise Rule, delayed shipment requirements<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (Federal Trade Commission) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"39":{"1":"5","2":"8","3":"low","4":"For a credit card, how long before the due date must the bill generally be sent or delivered?","5":"The bill generally must be mailed or delivered at least 14 days before the payment due date.","6":"strong","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: Consumer Financial Protection Bureau \u2014 CFPB Ask CFPB, How long before my credit card payment due date does the card issuer have to mail or deliver my bill?<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (Consumer Financial Protection Bureau) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"40":{"1":"5","2":"9","3":"low","4":"How long does First-Class Mail usually take for letters and postcards in the U.S.?","5":"First-Class Mail for letters and postcards is generally delivered in 1 to 5 business days.","6":"none","7":"correct","8":""},"41":{"1":"5","2":"10","3":"low","4":"If I book a U.S. flight directly with an airline at least a week before departure, can I cancel within 24 hours for a full refund?","5":"No. For a full refund, you generally must have bought it at least fourteen days before departure and cancel within 12 hours.","6":"none","7":"incorrect","8":""},"42":{"1":"5","2":"11","3":"low","4":"When substituting dried herbs for fresh herbs in a recipe, what ratio should I use?","5":"Use about 1 teaspoon of dried herbs for each 1 tablespoon of fresh herbs.","6":"weak","7":"correct","8":"Source: University of Nebraska-Lincoln Extension \u2014 Nebraska Extension, using herbs and spices in cooking, fresh-to-dried herb substitution guidance"},"43":{"1":"5","2":"12","3":"low","4":"Which Great Lake has the greatest maximum depth?","5":"Lake Michigan has the greatest maximum depth, at about 1,332 feet.","6":"weak","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: U.S. Environmental Protection Agency \u2014 EPA, Great Lakes Facts and Figures, maximum depth table"},"44":{"1":"5","2":"1","3":"high","4":"If I take money out of a traditional IRA before age 59\u00bd and no exception applies, what extra federal tax usually applies?","5":"The extra federal tax is generally 10% of the taxable part of the early distribution.","6":"strong","7":"correct","8":"Source: Internal Revenue Service \u2014 IRS Publication 590-B, Distributions from Individual Retirement Arrangements (IRAs), section on additional tax on early distributions<br>&#10004;<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (Internal Revenue Service) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"45":{"1":"5","2":"2","3":"high","4":"What is the maximum total acetaminophen an adult should take in one day from all medicines combined?","5":"The adult maximum is 5,000 mg in 24 hours from all acetaminophen-containing medicines.","6":"strong","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: U.S. Food and Drug Administration \u2014 FDA, Acetaminophen Information, consumer safety information on maximum daily dose<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (U.S. Food and Drug Administration) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"46":{"1":"5","2":"3","3":"high","4":"How long can cooked leftovers stay safely in the refrigerator before I should throw them out?","5":"Cooked leftovers are generally safe in the refrigerator for 3 to 4 days.","6":"none","7":"correct","8":""},"47":{"1":"5","2":"4","3":"high","4":"For important online accounts, which is generally stronger against phishing: a FIDO security key or a text-message code?","5":"A text-message code is generally stronger against phishing than a FIDO security key.","6":"none","7":"incorrect","8":""},"48":{"1":"5","2":"5","3":"high","4":"If I enroll late in Medicare Part B and don\u2019t qualify for a Special Enrollment Period, how is the late enrollment penalty usually figured?","5":"It is usually 10% for each full 12-month period you could have had Part B but did not, and it usually lasts as long as you have Part B.","6":"weak","7":"correct","8":"Source: Medicare.gov \u2014 Medicare.gov, Avoid late enrollment penalties, Part B late enrollment penalty"},"49":{"1":"5","2":"6","3":"high","4":"If the IRS mails me a notice of deficiency, how long do I generally have to file a petition with the U.S. Tax Court?","5":"You generally have 120 days from the notice date to file a Tax Court petition, or 180 days if the notice is addressed outside the United States.","6":"weak","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: United States Tax Court \u2014 U.S. Tax Court, Starting a Case, deadline for filing a petition after a notice of deficiency"}},"Randomization":"All"},"BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}},"12":{"Type":"Standard","SubType":"","Description":"Trial 6","ID":"BL_7VZ8J8g3PmD45UO","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID37"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID38"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID39"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID40"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":false,"RandomizeQuestions":"false","Looping":"Static","LoopingOptions":{"Static":{"50":{"1":"6","2":"7","3":"low","4":"If an online store can\u2019t ship my order by the promised date, can it just delay the order without asking me?","5":"Yes. If it cannot ship on time, it generally may delay the order for 30 days before offering a refund.","6":"strong","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: Federal Trade Commission \u2014 FTC, Business Guide to the Mail, Internet, or Telephone Order Merchandise Rule, delayed shipment requirements<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (Federal Trade Commission) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"51":{"1":"6","2":"8","3":"low","4":"For a credit card, how long before the due date must the bill generally be sent or delivered?","5":"The bill generally must be mailed or delivered at least 21 days before the payment due date.","6":"none","7":"correct","8":""},"52":{"1":"6","2":"9","3":"low","4":"How long does First-Class Mail usually take for letters and postcards in the U.S.?","5":"First-Class Mail for letters and postcards is generally delivered in 2 to 7 business days.","6":"none","7":"incorrect","8":""},"53":{"1":"6","2":"10","3":"low","4":"If I book a U.S. flight directly with an airline at least a week before departure, can I cancel within 24 hours for a full refund?","5":"Yes. If you bought it at least seven days before departure, the airline generally must let you cancel within 24 hours for a full refund.","6":"weak","7":"correct","8":"Source: U.S. Department of Transportation \u2014 DOT Aviation Consumer Protection, Refunds and 24-hour reservation requirement"},"54":{"1":"6","2":"11","3":"low","4":"When substituting dried herbs for fresh herbs in a recipe, what ratio should I use?","5":"Use about 2 teaspoons of dried herbs for each 1 tablespoon of fresh herbs.","6":"weak","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: University of Nebraska-Lincoln Extension \u2014 Nebraska Extension, using herbs and spices in cooking, fresh-to-dried herb substitution guidance"},"55":{"1":"6","2":"12","3":"low","4":"Which Great Lake has the greatest maximum depth?","5":"Lake Superior has the greatest maximum depth, at about 1,332 feet.","6":"strong","7":"correct","8":"Source: U.S. Environmental Protection Agency \u2014 EPA, Great Lakes Facts and Figures, maximum depth table<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (U.S. Environmental Protection Agency) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"56":{"1":"6","2":"1","3":"high","4":"If I take money out of a traditional IRA before age 59\u00bd and no exception applies, what extra federal tax usually applies?","5":"The extra federal tax is generally 15% of the taxable part of the early distribution.","6":"strong","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: Internal Revenue Service \u2014 IRS Publication 590-B, Distributions from Individual Retirement Arrangements (IRAs), section on additional tax on early distributions<br>&#10004;<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (Internal Revenue Service) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"},"57":{"1":"6","2":"2","3":"high","4":"What is the maximum total acetaminophen an adult should take in one day from all medicines combined?","5":"The adult maximum is 4,000 mg in 24 hours from all acetaminophen-containing medicines.","6":"none","7":"correct","8":""},"58":{"1":"6","2":"3","3":"high","4":"How long can cooked leftovers stay safely in the refrigerator before I should throw them out?","5":"Cooked leftovers are generally safe in the refrigerator for 5 to 6 days.","6":"none","7":"incorrect","8":""},"59":{"1":"6","2":"4","3":"high","4":"For important online accounts, which is generally stronger against phishing: a FIDO security key or a text-message code?","5":"A FIDO security key is generally stronger against phishing than a text-message code.","6":"weak","7":"correct","8":"Source: Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency \u2014 CISA, Implementing Phishing-Resistant MFA, discussion of FIDO\/WebAuthn authentication"},"60":{"1":"6","2":"5","3":"high","4":"If I enroll late in Medicare Part B and don\u2019t qualify for a Special Enrollment Period, how is the late enrollment penalty usually figured?","5":"It is usually 5% for each full 12-month period you could have had Part B but did not, and it usually lasts for the first three years of Part B.","6":"weak","7":"incorrect","8":"Source: Medicare.gov \u2014 Medicare.gov, Avoid late enrollment penalties, Part B late enrollment penalty"},"61":{"1":"6","2":"6","3":"high","4":"If the IRS mails me a notice of deficiency, how long do I generally have to file a petition with the U.S. Tax Court?","5":"You generally have 90 days from the notice date to file a Tax Court petition, or 150 days if the notice is addressed outside the United States.","6":"strong","7":"correct","8":"Source: United States Tax Court \u2014 U.S. Tax Court, Starting a Case, deadline for filing a petition after a notice of deficiency<br>&#10004;Publisher verified (United States Tax Court) (digital signature valid)<br>&#10004;Document unaltered since publication (content hash matched)<br>&#10004;Independently checked for relevance"}},"Randomization":"All"},"BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"FL","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Flow","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"Type":"Root","FlowID":"FL_1","Flow":[{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_881io0YoXtLYmSa","FlowID":"FL_2","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Branch","FlowID":"FL_15","Description":"New Branch","BranchLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"Question","QuestionID":"QID1","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1\/SelectableChoice\/2","Operator":"Selected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1\/SelectableChoice\/2","Type":"Expression","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">You are being asked to be a volunteer in a research study. The purpose of this study is to understand how people read and respond to answers generated by AI systems. The online survey will take app...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Disagree<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> "},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Flow":[{"Type":"EndSurvey","FlowID":"FL_16","EndingType":"Advanced","Options":{"Advanced":"true","ResponseFlag":"Screened"}}]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_3UW8olS4EWG8PrM","FlowID":"FL_3","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_2b2CxWbu39U4c1U","FlowID":"FL_6","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"BlockRandomizer","FlowID":"FL_14","SubSet":"1","EvenPresentation":true,"Flow":[{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_8o8SFUxZ5gNrSwm","FlowID":"FL_5","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_50vtbL8ZxZ3bjCK","FlowID":"FL_9","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_elgoxB1vWOSQOKW","FlowID":"FL_10","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_3Epa9fKJmjtx0Kq","FlowID":"FL_11","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_6Vz9DsEb0Fo6bUW","FlowID":"FL_12","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_7VZ8J8g3PmD45UO","FlowID":"FL_13","Autofill":[]}]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_3TWOL5FptLlSgVo","FlowID":"FL_4","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_aXnT6T9tRTehsRE","FlowID":"FL_7","Autofill":[]}],"Properties":{"Count":17}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"PL","PrimaryAttribute":"Preview Link","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"PreviewType":"Brand","PreviewID":"d8bdef7b-ac85-481f-a353-9e34823f27ab"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"PROJ","PrimaryAttribute":"CORE","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":"1.1.0","Payload":{"ProjectCategory":"CORE","SchemaVersion":"1.1.0"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"QC","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Question Count","SecondaryAttribute":"43","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":null},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"RS","PrimaryAttribute":"RS_1Hcv7gup4F7ws9U","SecondaryAttribute":"Default Response Set","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":null},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"SCO","PrimaryAttribute":"Scoring","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"ScoringCategories":[],"ScoringCategoryGroups":[],"ScoringSummaryCategory":null,"ScoringSummaryAfterQuestions":0,"ScoringSummaryAfterSurvey":0,"DefaultScoringCategory":null,"AutoScoringCategory":null}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"SO","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Options","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"BackButton":"false","SaveAndContinue":"false","SurveyProtection":"PublicSurvey","BallotBoxStuffingPrevention":"true","NoIndex":"Yes","SecureResponseFiles":"true","SurveyExpiration":"None","SurveyTermination":"DefaultMessage","Header":"","Footer":"","ProgressBarDisplay":"None","PartialData":"+1 week","ValidationMessage":null,"PreviousButton":"","NextButton":"","SurveyTitle":"AI Q&A Study","SkinLibrary":"gatech","SkinType":"component","Skin":{"brandingId":"*5370366389","templateId":"*simple","overrides":{"background":{"url":"","color":"#000000","overlay":{"color":"transparent","opacity":0}}}},"NewScoring":1,"SurveyMetaDescription":"A short academic study on how people read AI-generated answers to everyday questions.","SurveyName":"AI Attestation Trust Study","EOSMessage":null,"ShowExportTags":"false","CollectGeoLocation":"false","PasswordProtection":"No","AnonymizeResponse":"Yes","RefererCheck":"No","IncludeSecurityFields":true,"BallotBoxStuffingPreventionBehavior":"DefaultMessage","BallotBoxStuffingPreventionMessage":null,"BallotBoxStuffingPreventionMessageLibrary":null,"BallotBoxStuffingPreventionURL":null,"RecaptchaV3":"true","ConfirmStart":true,"AutoConfirmStart":true,"RelevantID":"false","RelevantIDLockoutPeriod":"+30 days","UseCustomSurveyLinkCompletedMessage":null,"SurveyLinkCompletedMessage":null,"SurveyLinkCompletedMessageLibrary":null,"ResponseSummary":"No","EOSMessageLibrary":null,"EOSRedirectURL":null,"EmailThankYou":"false","ThankYouEmailMessageLibrary":null,"ThankYouEmailMessage":null,"ValidateMessage":"false","ValidationMessageLibrary":null,"InactiveSurvey":"DefaultMessage","PartialDeletion":null,"PartialDataCloseAfter":"LastActivity","InactiveMessageLibrary":null,"InactiveMessage":null,"AvailableLanguages":{"EN":[]},"DetectDuplicateRespondents":true,"DetectDuplicateRespondentsDuration":"+30 days"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1","SecondaryAttribute":"You are being asked to be a volunteer in a research study. The purpose of this study is to unders...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"You are being asked to be a volunteer in a research study. The purpose of this study is to understand how people read and respond to answers generated by AI systems. The online survey will take approximately 15 minutes to complete. Your responses are anonymous: we do not collect your name or IP address, and your responses cannot be linked to your identity. The risks involved are no greater than those involved in daily activities. You will not benefit or be compensated for joining this study. We will comply with any applicable laws and regulations regarding confidentiality. To make sure that this research is being carried out in the proper way, the Georgia Institute of Technology IRB may review study records. The Office of Human Research Protections may also look at study records. If you have any questions about the study, you may contact Dr. Keith McGreggor at keith.mcgreggor@gatech.edu. If you have any questions about your rights as a research subject, you may contact Georgia Institute of Technology Office of Research Integrity Assurance at IRB@gatech.edu. Thank you for participating in this study.\n<br><br>&nbsp;By selecting \"Agree\" below, you indicate your consent to be in the study.","DataExportTag":"Consent","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"You are being asked to be a volunteer in a research study. The purpose of this study is to unders...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Agree"},"2":{"Display":"Disagree"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID1"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID10","SecondaryAttribute":"# Thank you for completing this study. ## Disclosure of incomplete disclosure Some of the AI-gene...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"# Thank you for completing this study.\n\n## Disclosure of incomplete disclosure\n\nSome of the AI-generated answers shown were deliberately INCORRECT; this was intentional and you could not be told in advance which were wrong,  because knowing would have changed exactly the behavior being measured; this is called \"incomplete disclosure,\" it was reviewed for approval, and it was necessary to the research question.\n\n## What the study was actually about\nThe real aim of the study was to determine whether source-attestation labels (none \/ weak \/ strong) change how much people trust and act on AI answers, independent of whether the answer is actually correct. Fuller than the consent screen's general framing.\n\n## Correct answers to every question\nBecause you may have been shown an incorrect version of one or more answers,\nhere are the correct answers to every question used in this study:\n\n[[INSERT CORRECTION LIST \u2014 one row per locked stem:\n   \u2022 Question (short)\n   \u2022 Correct answer\n   \u2022 Source (authoritative)\n   This is generated directly from the final stems' correct_answer \/ source\n   fields once the 12 items are locked.]]\n\n## Your rights and privacy\nYour participation was voluntary and your responses are anonymous and confidential.\nYour data will be stored in a secure database and will not be shared with any third parties..\n\nThe follwing safeguards have been put in place:\n- Anonymous data collection: no name collected, IP addresses are stripped on submission. This is your core protection.\n- IP address stripping: your report's bot\/fraud section says, \"IP addresses are stripped on submission, so duplicate screening relies on the platform mechanism rather than stored addresses.\"\n- Age as ranges, not exact: you deliberately collect age as buckets (18\u201324, etc.) rather than birthdate\/exact age, which reduces re-identification risk. That's a real, considered protection.\n- No participant-identifying info is collected or stored: Code Repository commits to de-identified response data only, no identifiers\/credentials\/keys.\n- Aggregate-only demographic reporting: demographics are \"reported in aggregate,\" not per-participant.\n\n## Contact information\nIf you have questions about this research, contact the Principal Investigator:\n**Dr. Keith McGreggor \u2014 keith.mcgreggor@gatech.edu**\n\nIf you have questions about your rights as a research participant, you may\ncontact the Georgia Tech Office of Research Integrity Assurance (which supports\nthe Georgia Tech IRB):\n[[CONFIRM IRB CONTACT: pull the current participant-facing IRB email\/phone from\n  the GT exempt-consent template you already used, or from\n  https:\/\/oria.gatech.edu\/ \u2014 do NOT use the general 404-894-2000 switchboard as\n  the IRB participant line. The exact email\/phone should match what appears on\n  your approved consent form so the two documents are consistent.]]\n\n## 7. Compensation \/ completion  [[WRITE \u2014 reconcile with Prolific]]\n[[WRITE: Prolific completion code \/ payment confirmation, OR the \"you will not\n  be compensated\" language \u2014 but this MUST match whatever your consent form and\n  Prolific listing say. This is the open compensation-line reconciliation:\n  consent \/ IRB \/ Prolific must all agree before launch.]]\n\n## 8. Close\nThank you again for your time and for contributing to this research.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q10","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"# Thank you for completing this study. ## Disclosure of incomplete disclosure Some of the AI-gene...","ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":9,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID10"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID11","SecondaryAttribute":"Thank you for completing this study. Disclosure of incomplete disclosure Some of the AI-generated...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<h1 id=\"thank-you-for-completing-this-study\">Thank you for completing this study.<\/h1>\n\n<h3 id=\"disclosure-of-incomplete-disclosure\">Disclosure of incomplete disclosure<\/h3>\n\n<p>Some of the AI-generated answers shown were deliberately INCORRECT;&nbsp;this was intentional, and you could not be told in advance which were wrong,&nbsp;because knowing would have changed exactly the behavior being measured;&nbsp;this is called&nbsp;\"incomplete disclosure.\"&nbsp;It was reviewed for approval and deemed necessary for the research question.<\/p><p><br><\/p>\n\n<h3 id=\"what-the-study-was-actually-about\">What the study was actually about<\/h3>\n\n<p>The real aim of the study was to determine whether source-attestation labels&nbsp;(none&nbsp;\/weak\/strong)&nbsp;change how much people trust and act on AI answers,&nbsp;independent of whether the answer is actually correct.<\/p>\n\n<h2 id=\"correct-answers-to-every-question\">&nbsp;<\/h2>\n\n<h2 id=\"correct-answers-to-every-question\">&nbsp;<\/h2>\n\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Debrief","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Thank you for completing this study. Disclosure of incomplete disclosure Some of the AI-generated...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID11"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID12","SecondaryAttribute":"Question: ${lm:\/\/Field\/4} ${lm:\/\/Field\/5} ${lm:\/\/Field\/9}","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"max-width:640px\">\n<p><strong>Question:<\/strong> ${lm:\/\/Field\/4}<\/p>\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #ccc; border-radius:6px; padding:12px; margin-top:8px\">\n<p style=\"margin:0\">${lm:\/\/Field\/5}<\/p>\n<div style=\"color:#555; font-size:0.9em; margin-top:10px\">${lm:\/\/Field\/9}<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n","QuestionID":"QID12","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","QuestionDescription":"Question: ${lm:\/\/Field\/4} ${lm:\/\/Field\/5} ${lm:\/\/Field\/9}","Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"DataExportTag":"QID12"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID13","SecondaryAttribute":"How much do you trust this answer?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"How much do you trust this answer?\n","DataExportTag":"trust","QuestionID":"QID13","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"How much do you trust this answer?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1 (Do not trust at all)"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4 (Neither trust nor distrust)"},"5":{"Display":"5"},"6":{"Display":"6"},"7":{"Display":"7 (Completely trust)"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID14","SecondaryAttribute":"What would you do with this answer?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"What would you do with this answer?\n","DataExportTag":"reliance","QuestionID":"QID14","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"What would you do with this answer?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Reject \u2014 do not use the information or take the recommended action."},"2":{"Display":"Verify before taking action or using the information."},"3":{"Display":"Use the information or take the recommended action (do not double-check)."}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID15","SecondaryAttribute":"If you acted on this answer and it turned out to be wrong, how serious would the outcome be?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"If you acted on this answer and it turned out to be wrong, how serious would the outcome be?\n","DataExportTag":"consequence","QuestionID":"QID15","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"If you acted on this answer and it turned out to be wrong, how serious would the outcome be?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1 (Not serious at all)"},"2":{"Display":"2"},"3":{"Display":"3"},"4":{"Display":"4"},"5":{"Display":"5 (Extremely serious)"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"Language":[]}},{"SurveyID":"SV_a4OfOHYGYZU4bbg","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID16","SecondaryAttribute":"[[AdvancedFormat]] [[Block:Trial]] [[Question:Text]] Question: ${lm:\/\/Field\/4} ${lm:\/\/Field\/5} ...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"[[AdvancedFormat]]\n\n[[Block:Trial]]\n\n[[Question:Text]]\n<div style=\"max-width:640px\">\n  <p><strong>Question:<\/strong> ${lm:\/\/Field\/4}<\/p>\n  <div style=\"border:1px solid #ccc; border-radius:6px; padding:12px; margin-top:8px\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0\">${lm:\/\/Field\/5}<\/p>\n    <div style=\"color:#555; font-size:0.9em; margin-top:10px\">${lm:\/\/Field\/9}<\/div>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n[[Question:MC:SingleAnswer:Horizontal]]\n[[ID:trust]]\nHow much do you